 <h1>A Guide to Baking Brownies</h1>
    <p>A guide to bake classic, rich, and fudgy home made brownies.</p>

<hr />

   <h2>Essential ingredients</h2>
     <h3>Wet ingerdients</h3>
       <ul>
          <li>1/2 cup of Un-salted buttter </li>
          <li>2 Eggs</li>
          <li>One teaspoon of pure vanilla extract</li>
       </ul>

     <h3>Dry ingredients</h3>
       <ul>
          <li>1 cup of granulated white sugar</li>
          <li>1/3 cup of un-sweetened cocoa powder</li>
          <li>1/2 cup of all-purpose flower</li>
          <li>1/4 teaspoon salt</li>
          <li>1/4 teaspoon baking powder</li>
       </ul>

<hr />

    <h2>Step-By-Step Instructions</h2>  
  <ol>
    <li><h3>Preheat and Prep</h3></li>
           <p> Heat your oven to 350°F or 175°C. Line an 8x8-inch metal baking pan with parchment paper, leaving a little overhang for a easy removal.</p>
    <li><h3>Melt the Butter</h3></li>
           <p>Place the 1/2 cup of un-salted butter in a bowl, then melt it in the microwave. After let it cool for 2-3 minutes.</p>    
    <li><h3>Mix Butter and Sugar</h3></li>
           <p>Pour the warm melted butter into a large mixing bowl, then add the white sugar and wisk vigorously untill smooth and glossy.</p>
    <li><h3>Add Wet Ingredients</h3></li>
           <p>Whisk the 2 large eggs and 1 teaspoon of vanilla extarct untill the mixture looks uniform and slightly thick.</p>
    <li><h3>Combine Dry Ingerdients</h3></li>
           <p>Sift in the ⅓ cup cocoa powder, ½ cup all-purpose flour, ¼ teaspoon salt, and ¼ teaspoon baking powder.</p>
    <li><h3>Fold the Batter</h3></li>
           <p> Gently stir with a spatula just until the flour disappears. Do not overmix, or the brownies will turn out cakey instead of fudgy.</p>
    <li><h3>Bake</h3></li>
           <p>Spread the batter evenly into your prepared pan. Bake on the center rack for 20 to 25 minutes. A toothpick inserted into the center should come out with a few moist crumbs attached.</p>
    <li><h3>Let it Rest</h3></li>
           <p>Remove from the pan after baking and let it rest on a wire rack for about 10-15 minutes.</p>
  </ol>
 
